<title>UK: GOLF-LEHMAN UP TO SECOND, MONTY DROPS TO SIXTH.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEHMAN UP TO SECOND, MONTY DROPS TO SIXTH.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Open champion Tom Lehman's</p>
<p>victory in the U.S. Tour Championship on Monday boosted him five</p>
<p>positions to second place behind Greg Norman in the world</p>
<p>rankings.</p>
<p>Colin Montgomerie's joint 29th place finish in the European</p>
<p>Tour equivalent event, the Volvo Masters in Valderrama, dropped</p>
<p>him five places from second to sixth, according to the new list</p>
<p>released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mark McNulty of Zimbabwe, who won the Volvo Masters, moved</p>
<p>up from 31st to 24th place.</p>
<p> 1. Greg Norman (Australia)     10.22 points average</p>
